    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Structural pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 1</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Decorator</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Add features to one object at run time by wrapping it in another object with the same interface, and stack as many wrappers as you like. The standard answer for coffee and pizza pricing, the design behind Java I/O streams, and the same idea as stacking dm-crypt on top of a disk.</p>\n"
